# audio_system.md

This document defines the **Audio System** for *Purge of the Crescent Veil*.

**Note:** All systems are modular and self-contained. See [docs/modular/game_system_tree.md](../modular/game_system_tree.md) for the latest status. A system remains **In-Progress** until its documentation, cleanup, and tests are merged and verified.


The engine previously used an `[REDACTED]` built on OpenAL Soft. That
component has been removed and audio is now generated purely through the
`[REDACTED]` module.

---

## Core Concepts

- Audio is a key driver of **tone and immersion**.
- Audio systems must support:
    - Dynamic music
    - Faction-based sound cues
    - Combat feedback
    - Narrator voice system
    - Space Combat audio integration

---

## Music System

- Dynamic layer-based soundtrack
- Multiple music channels: ambient, combat and boss
- Alignment-reactive music states
- Channel mixing overlays ambient/combat/boss themes
- Faction-controlled stage music variants
- Boss intro music triggers
- Space Combat music (distinct layer)
- Independent ambient/combat/boss layers can play together

---

## Sound Effects

- Faction-based weapon sounds
- Faith/Corruption power effects
- Environmental audio (stage corruption, storm events)
- Alignment-reactive ambient cues
- Hub ambient audio (alignment state driven)

---

## Narrator System

- Multiple narrator personalities:
    - Drill sergeant (Empire military chapters)
    - Inquisitor (Empire Order chapters)
    - Veil priest (Crescent Veil chapters)
    - Skitterkin chieftain (Skitterkin factions, future)

- Narrator commentary driven by:
    - Alignment state
    - Combat events
    - Stage progression
    - Narrative choices
- VO channels are exposed for future multi-narrator support

---

## Space Combat Audio

- Distinct space combat sound layer
- Ship weapon sounds
- Space ambient audio
- Space-based narrator commentary (planned)

---

## Current Features

- Channel mixing overlays ambient/combat/boss music
- Alignment-based modulation hooks
- [REDACTED] modulation hooks adjust [REDACTED] track volumes
- Multiple buffers can play simultaneously on each music channel
- Alignment values cross-fade volumes between ambient, combat and boss tracks
- Voice channel management for multi-narrator support

### Procedural Synth Engine
- `[REDACTED]` generates real-time waveforms using sine, square, saw, triangle and noise shapes.
- `[REDACTED]` queues synthesized notes.
- Gameplay systems trigger effects via helper methods such as `[REDACTED]` and `[REDACTED]`.
